sample:
 Here is how you can create and use a Material UI (MUI) theme in a React app:

1. Install Material UI and its peer dependencies:

```
npm install @mui/material @mui/styled-engine-sc styled-components
```

2. Create a theme file (e.g. theme.js) and define your theme:

```jsx
import { createTheme } from '@mui/material/styles'; 

const theme = createTheme({
  palette: {
    primary: {
      main: '#556cd6',
    },
  },
});

export default theme;
```

3. Wrap your App component with the ThemeProvider and pass the theme:

```jsx
// App.js
import { ThemeProvider } from '@mui/material/styles';
import theme from './theme';

function App() {
  return (
    <ThemeProvider theme={theme}>
      <Root />
    </ThemeProvider>
  );
}
```

4. Use the theme in your components:

```jsx
// Button.js
import Button from '@mui/material/Button';

export default function MyButton() {
  return <Button color="primary">My Button</Button>; 
}
```

The Button will now use the primary color from the theme. You can customize the theme further by changing palette colors, typography, breakpoints etc.

