• Lets you access native APIs like Touch ID, sensors, camera, etc.

• Hot reloading enables you to instantly see changes without recompiling native code.

• Cross-platform - code written using React Native works on both Android and iOS. You just compile it for each platform.

• Large ecosystem of third party libraries and tools.

• Backed by Facebook and the open-source community.

A basic React Native app structure would be:

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { View, Text } from 'react-native';

function App() {
  return (
    <View>
      <Text>Hello world!</Text>
    </View>
  );
}

export default App; 
```

This lets you build mobile apps with fast development turnaround and a consistent experience on both platforms.

So in summary, React Native lets you quickly build mobile apps using React and native platform components.

