CodeIgniter is a popular PHP framework for building dynamic websites. Some of its main features are:

• Lightweight but robust - CodeIgniter is a small framework but still very capable.

• Simple syntax - CodeIgniter uses a simple syntax with easy to read code.

• Modular structure - CodeIgniter apps have a modular structure which makes the framework flexible and easy to work with.

• Database abstraction - CodeIgniter has a database abstraction layer which supports multiple databases.

• Security - CodeIgniter has built-in security features to help prevent vulnerabilities and hacking.

• Templating engine - CodeIgniter has a simple templating engine for generating views.

• Routing - CodeIgniter has a routing system to map URLs to controllers and functions.

• Caching - CodeIgniter has caching capabilities to improve performance.

• And more - CodeIgniter has many other features like sessions, validation, file uploading, etc.

Some examples of using CodeIgniter:

```php
// Controller
class Welcome extends CI_Controller {
    public function index() {
        $this->load->view('welcome_message'); 
    }
}

// View (welcome_message.php)
<h1>Welcome!</h1>
<p>This is a CodeIgniter view!</p>
```

So in summary, CodeIgniter is a popular, lightweight PHP framework for building dynamic websites and web apps.

